      "side": 1,
      "message": "I removed the shouldNotify boolean and went back to using a STOPPING state. This is necessary to handle the following sequence of events: start, stop, interface up. And not send a LinkProperties update in that case.\n\n\u003e - 464xlat is what knows when the interface is removed, so it should be\n   responsible for telling CS when that happens.\n\nDone: notification is always sent if the interface is removed.\n\n\u003e CS is responsible for ensuring that if external classes call\n   its handleUpdateLinkProperties public method, it doesn\u0027t behave incorrectly\n\n\nDone in ConnectivityService",
